      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-25T00:10:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have you thought about having one struct definition for all device classes (drp_acc_trysrc, ctvpd, vpd) in a hierarchical way? We should use structs to group related fields. There are common fields between ctvpd and vpd, for example. VPD fields should be just shared between VPD and CTVPD class.\n\nRoughly speaking, I\u0027m expecting something like:\n\n  struct type_c {\n     struct sm_obj obj;\n     ... common fields ...\n     struct vpd {\n        struct charge_through ct;\n        ... fields common in vpd and ctvpd ...\n     } vpd;\n     struct drp_acc_try_src drp;\n  }\n\nWhat\u0027s the design rationale about this flat \u0026 duplicated struct?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "84b915262e850ef85e0f4aa72d23b12142926f6c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
